clean:
  browsers sign in: browser (sign-in /sign-in, sign-out /sign-out, 1800 s, origin from Host)
behind a proxy:
  browsers sign in: browser (sign-in /sign-in, sign-out /sign-out, 1800 s, origin https://notes.example)
sign-in page needs a user:
  browsers sign in: browser (sign-in /sign-in, sign-out /sign-out, 1800 s, origin from Host)
  posting to the sign-in path /sign-in needs a user, so nobody could sign in
plain HTTP, and test_users:
  browsers sign in: browser (sign-in /sign-in, sign-out /sign-out, 1800 s, origin http://localhost:8080)
  the session cookie is sent over plain HTTP (origin http://localhost:8080)
  test_users is accepted
